    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1185">

                <pb facs="1020" n="916" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg916"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.94/1b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Japanese
                        Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I desire to inform you
                    that after your call on Friday the 26th instant the Department sent telegraphic
                    instructions to the Consul of the United States at Chihuahua to use his good
                    offices in behalf of Japanese subjects as he had done in the case of other
                    aliens.</p>
                <p>The Department has also taken up with the Department of Labor the question of
                    affording temporary refuge at El Paso to Japanese subjects in case they should
                    be obliged to leave Chihuahua.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
